===BODY===
          <h2>Winter breakdowns in the Alps</h2>
          <p>Cold starts, flat batteries, snow chains and steep mountain roads make winter the busiest time for breakdowns in Austria, especially in Tyrol and around Salzburg. A local recovery service usually takes the car to a garage first. From there we collect it and bring it home.</p>

          <h2>Where we collect from</h2>
          <p>We collect from all over Austria: Innsbruck and the Tyrolean resorts, Salzburg and the Salzburger Land, Vienna, Graz, Linz and the routes over the Brenner Pass, as long as the car is somewhere a transporter can reach.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Good to know:</strong> Austrian motorways need a vignette, and winter tyres or chains are required in wintry conditions. If you're driving on after a breakdown in a hire car, check the rules for your route.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>How it works</h2>
          <p>Send us the location, the make and model, whether it runs, and the UK delivery address. We quote one fixed price for the whole journey, collect the car on a transporter and bring it back through Germany, Belgium and France to the Channel.</p>
===FAQ===
Q: Can you collect from a ski resort in Austria?
A: Usually, yes, as long as the car is somewhere a transporter can reach safely. Tell us exactly where it is and we'll confirm.
Q: How long does it take?
A: It's a long journey, and timing depends on the location and the season. We'll give you an expected collection and delivery time with the quote.
Q: Can my insurance cover the repatriation?
A: Many European breakdown policies include it. Check with your insurer. If you need to arrange it yourself, we'll give you a written quote.
